# For docker/Dockerfile, which builds from this checkout with the repository root
# as its context:  docker build -f docker/Dockerfile .
#
# An allow-list rather than a deny-list. A working checkout carries hundreds of
# megabytes the image never reads — third_party/cef alone is ~350 MB, plus build/
# and the plugin's tree — and COPY layers are keyed on what they are given, so a
# docs edit that reached the context would rebuild Chromium's wrapper for
# nothing. Keep this in step with the COPY lines in docker/Dockerfile and the
# path filter in .github/workflows/docker.yml.
*
!CMakeLists.txt
!cmake
!src
!tests
!third_party
third_party/cef
!docker/docker-entrypoint.sh
!docker/healthcheck.sh
